    "sl_custom_faq_r7Q6ht": {
      "type": "sl-custom-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_qjMHfp": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will I actually peel and have downtime after my treatment?",
            "answer": "<p>With our PCA chemical peels, most clients experience little to no visible peeling. You may notice some light flaking that's easily managed with moisturizer, but nothing that would keep you from going about your normal life. These are truly no downtime peels — you can return to work, social events, and daily activities immediately.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_PzXEKn": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How many treatments will I need to see results?",
            "answer": "<p>While you'll see some improvement after your very first chemical peel, optimal results come from a series of treatments. We typically recommend 3 to 6 peels spaced 3 to 4 weeks apart, depending on your skin goals. During your consultation, we'll create a personalized treatment plan that fits your needs and budget.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_GmWhMf": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do chemical peels hurt?",
            "answer": "<p>Our PCA chemical peels are designed to be gentle yet effective. Most clients describe the sensation as a mild tingling or warmth during application. Any sensation subsides quickly, and many clients find the treatment surprisingly relaxing. If you have sensitive skin, we'll adjust your peel formula accordingly.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_PGh67J": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are chemical peels safe for my skin type and tone?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes! One of the biggest advantages of PCA chemical peels is that they can be customized for virtually any skin type, tone, and concern. Whether you have dry, oily, sensitive, or combination skin — and regardless of your skin tone — we'll blend a peel that's perfect for you. That's why we offer the Pre-Peel Consultation for first-timers.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_XkqtLR": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "question": "When will I see results from my chemical peel?",
            "answer": "<p>You'll notice an immediate glow after your first chemical peel treatment. Over the following days, your skin will continue to improve as cell turnover accelerates. For concerns like dark spots, fine lines, and texture issues, visible improvement typically continues for 2-4 weeks after each treatment, with cumulative benefits building over your peel series.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_P6KPXe": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's the difference between professional chemical peels and drugstore peels?",
            "answer": "<p>Professional PCA chemical peels use higher concentrations of active ingredients that simply aren't available over the counter. More importantly, we custom-blend each peel for your specific skin — combining different acids and ingredients to target your unique concerns. Drugstore peels are one-size-fits-all; ours are one-of-a-kind, just like your skin.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
